I"¦<h2 id="the-question">The question</h2>

<p>Many people with type 2 diabetes are prescribed antidepressants or antipsychotics. Do these medicines affect how their diabetes goes?</p>

<h2 id="what-we-did">What we did</h2>

<p>As part of a PhD project, we carried out a systematic review, which means searching and appraising the research in a structured way, of observational studies on antidepressant or antipsychotic prescribing and diabetes outcomes.</p>

<h2 id="what-we-found">What we found</h2>

<p>Studies on this question are scarce, have shortcomings and give mixed findings. There is not enough evidence yet to say how these drugs affect diabetes outcomes.</p>

<h2 id="why-it-matters">Why it matters</h2>

<p>Until better evidence arrives, people with diabetes who are prescribed these medicines should receive the monitoring, risk-factor treatment and complication screening recommended in general diabetes guidelines.</p>
